      "text": "1. Let \\( DC = x \\). Then, \\( PC = x + 6 \\) and \\( PB = x + 7 \\).\n2. Given that \\(\\triangle PAB \\sim \\triangle PCA\\), we can use the Angle-Angle (AA) similarity criterion. This means that the corresponding angles of the two triangles must be equal. Specifically, \\(\\angle BAP = \\angle CAP\\) and \\(\\angle ABP = \\angle ACP\\).\n3. Using the similarity, we can set up the following proportion based on the sides of the triangles:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{PB}{PC} = \\frac{AB}{AC} \\implies \\frac{x + 7}{x + 6} = \\frac{8}{6} = \\frac{4}{3}\n   \\]\n4. Solving the proportion for \\( x \\):\n   \\[\n   \\frac{x + 7}{x + 6} = \\frac{4}{3}\n   \\]\n   Cross-multiplying gives:\n   \\[\n   3(x + 7) = 4(x + 6)\n   \\]\n   Expanding both sides:\n   \\[\n   3x + 21 = 4x + 24\n   \\]\n   Rearranging terms to isolate \\( x \\):\n   \\[\n   21 - 24 = 4x - 3x \\implies -3 = x\n   \\]\n5. Therefore, \\( DC = x = 3 \\) and \\( PC = x + 6 = 3 + 6 = 9 \\).\n6. The length of \\( PC \\) is \\(\\boxed{9}\\).",
