      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to use the properties of similar triangles. Given that \\(\\triangle PAB \\sim \\triangle PCA\\), we can set up a proportion based on the corresponding sides of the triangles.\n\nLet's denote the length of \\(PC\\) as \\(x\\). According to the similarity of \\(\\triangle PAB\\) and \\(\\triangle PCA\\), we have the following proportion:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{PA}{PC} = \\frac{AB}{CA}\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the given side lengths, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{PA}{x} = \\frac{8}{6} = \\frac{4}{3}\n\\]\n\nFrom this, we can solve for \\(PA\\):\n\n\\[\nPA = \\frac{4}{3}x\n\\]\n\nNext, we use the triangle inequality theorem to find the possible range for \\(x\\). The triangle inequality theorem states that the sum of the lengths of any two sides of a triangle must be greater than the length of the remaining side.\n\nFor \\(\\triangle PAB\\):\n\n\\[\nPA + AB > PB \\implies \\frac{4}{3}x + 8 > PB\n\\]\n\nFor \\(\\triangle PCA\\):\n\n\\[\nPA + CA > PC \\implies \\frac{4}{3}x + 6 > x \\implies \\frac{4}{3}x - x > -6 \\implies -\\frac{1}{3}x > -6 \\implies x < 18\n\\]\n\nFor \\(\\triangle PAB\\) and \\(\\triangle PCA\\) to be valid triangles, \\(PB\\) must be positive and less than the sum of the other two sides.\n\nFor \\(\\triangle PCA\\):\n\n\\[\nPA + CA > PC \\implies \\frac{4}{3}x + 6 > x \\implies \\frac{4}{3}x - x > -6 \\implies -\\frac{1}{3}x > -6 \\implies x < 18\n\\]\n\nCombining these inequalities, we get:\n\n\\[\n6 < x < 18\n\\]\n\nSince \\(x\\) must be an integer, the only possible value that fits within this range is \\(x = 9\\).\n\nTo verify, we check the sides of \\(\\triangle PCA\\) with \\(PC = 9\\):\n\n\\[\nPA = \\frac{4}{3} \\times 9 = 12\n\\]\n\n\\[\nPB = PA + AB = 12 + 8 = 20\n\\]\n\n\\[\nPC = 9\n\\]\n\nWe check the triangle inequalities:\n\n1. \\(PA + PB > PC \\implies 12 + 20 > 9 \\implies 32 > 9\\) (True)\n2. \\(PA + PC > PB \\implies 12 + 9 > 20 \\implies 21 > 20\\) (True)\n3. \\(PC + PB > PA \\implies 9 + 20 > 12 \\implies 29 > 12\\) (True)\n\nAll conditions are satisfied, so the length of \\(PC\\) is indeed \\(9\\).\n\nThus, the correct option is \\(\\boxed{9}\\).",
